{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on question 1bd1f48f, identifiers (c+d): the entry records the\nkind. A scope never needs a remote read, or a cache hit, to read its\nown retained entries.\n\nWhy. The first branch leaves a scope unable to read a field of its own\nretained delivery after a restart or an eviction, unless it reads the\nsender again. A judgment over the scope's own head then depends on\nanother scope's availability. Kernel promise 4 forbids that. The old\nentry held this fact: `from.at` carried the kind. The cutover removed\nit from the reference, and section 8 says that the receiver \"reads that\ngenesis once and holds it\". The durable holder is the entry.\n\n1. The record. An entry whose judgment chose a handler or a rule by\n   the kind of a sender records that kind: a delivery entry for the\n   sequence of its `from`, and a genesis entry for the sequence of its\n   `source`. It is one ScopeKind value. The receiving scope writes it\n   when it seals the entry, from the checked genesis of ruling\n   79439167. It never comes from the wire, a reference, a name or a\n   pin. It lies inside the hashed bytes of the entry and outside the\n   seed. Propose the exact member in the core construction, and state\n   what it does to the `artroom-input-1` digest.\n2. The consumers. `bound` and its four callers, and `operand.fieldOf`,\n   read the recorded kind of the retained entry. They read nothing\n   else and return no empty proof for a missing kind. A new-format\n   delivery or created genesis without the member is malformed: the\n   scope does not seal it, and Replay reports it.\n3. Replay. With the verified genesis of the sender in hand, Replay\n   compares, and a difference is a mismatch. Without it, Replay judges\n   with the recorded kind, and one trust row says so: the kind that an\n   entry records for a sender whose genesis Replay did not read. The\n   recorded kind never makes a CheckedSequence, a birth proof or\n   `from.pin` evidence.\n4. Privacy and floor. The member is one kind word about a sequence\n   that the entry already names. It follows the entry through floors\n   and archives with no rule of its own.\n\nA question back, before more caller-record code. With item 3, the\ndelivery sender and the creation source need no caller record in\noffline Replay. Read the core inventory and tell me which sites of\nruling 429c1be7 still need a kind that no replayed entry records. I\nexpect only the source of a named fact use and the membership of a\ngrant. Say how the entry lists those uses today. If each use row can\nrecord its verified kind in the same way, I withdraw the caller record\nof 70186a25 and 608503ab, and `--trust-published-anchors` supplies\nanchors alone. Until you answer, keep the shared Replay seam and hold\nthe caller-record plumbing at its present source.\n\nThe cache ruling stands for admission. The archive root ruling\n33c2c7c7 stands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}